+// Fogata: the ceiling over which the capture ends the second after a partial
+// reset is the loudest ratio recorded in the half second (125 updates) before
+// the reset, not the loudest of the last 125 recorded. Here the far end is
+// quiet for most of that half second (a silent capture, left out of the ratios
+// as a weak render is), so the last 125 recorded ratios reach back into the
+// near end's talk before it. The echo alone, louder than the pauses, is still
+// not taken for talk after the reset; the near end talking again is, at once.
+TEST(MatchedFilter, PartialResetCeilingIsOnlyTheHalfSecondBeforeIt) {
+  constexpr float kTalk = ExactLevelNearTalk::kTalkAmplitude;
+  // 10 dB over the pauses: talk to the filter (more than 8 dB) but for the
+  // second.
+  const float echo =
